#: ../../tests/package-data.md:136
msgid "Store Your Data in a Scientific Repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:138
msgid ""
"Scientific data repositories offer reliable, long-term storage for "
"research datasets. These platforms are typically free and provide "
"essential features like DOIs and version control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:140
msgid "Some popular places to store data include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:142
msgid ""
"**[Zenodo](https://zenodo.org)** - General-purpose repository with "
"excellent GitHub integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:143
msgid ""
"**[Open Science Framework (OSF)](https://osf.io)** - Comprehensive "
"research platform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:144
msgid ""
"**[Figshare](https://figshare.com)** - User-friendly with good "
"visualization tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:145
msgid ""
"**[Dryad](https://datadryad.org)** - Focused on research data "
"(subscription model for some features)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:147
msgid "Pros and Cons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:149
msgid "**Strengths:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:151
msgid "**Free to use** - No cost for most repositories and storage limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:152
msgid ""
"**Guaranteed long-term preservation** - Data remains accessible "
"indefinitely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:153
msgid ""
"**DOI assignment** - Permanent identifiers make datasets citable in "
"publications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:154
msgid "**Version control** - Track changes and maintain multiple dataset versions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:155
msgid ""
"**Community standards** - Well-suited for pyOpenSci packages and research"
" workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:157
msgid "**Weaknesses:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:159
msgid ""
"**Limited automation** - Difficult to set up automated uploads for "
"dynamic datasets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:160
msgid "**Static nature** - Not designed for frequently changing or real-time data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:162
msgid "Private Cloud Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:164
msgid ""
"Private cloud platforms offer scalable, enterprise-grade storage with "
"extensive automation capabilities. These services provide robust "
"infrastructure and comprehensive tooling for data management workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:166
msgid "Pros and cons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:168
msgid "There are some pros to using private cloud storage for your data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:170
msgid ""
"**Robust infrastructure** - Enterprise-grade reliability and uptime "
"guarantees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:171
msgid ""
"**Automation-friendly** - Rich APIs and tooling for automated data "
"pipelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:172
msgid "**Scalability** - Handle datasets from gigabytes to petabytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:173
msgid ""
"**Integration capabilities** - Connect with CI/CD pipelines and package "
"management systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:174
msgid ""
"**Advanced features** - Access controls, encryption, backup, and disaster"
" recovery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:176
msgid "And also some cons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:178
msgid "**Cost** - Pay-per-use pricing can become expensive for large datasets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:179
msgid ""
"**Technical complexity** - Requires cloud infrastructure knowledge and "
"setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:180
msgid "**Vendor lock-in** - May create dependencies on specific cloud ecosystems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:182
msgid "Popular Platforms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:184
msgid ""
"**[Amazon Web Services (AWS)](https://aws.amazon.com/s3/)** - S3 storage "
"with extensive ecosystem integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:185
msgid ""
"**[Google Cloud Platform](https://cloud.google.com/storage)** - Cloud "
"Storage with strong AI/ML tool integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:186
msgid ""
"**[Linode](https://www.linode.com/products/object-storage/)** - Object "
"Storage with straightforward pricing and developer-friendly tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:188
msgid "Version control platforms for your data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:191
msgid ""
"Platforms exist that allow you to track changes to datasets in the same "
"way as version control systems like git let you track changes to code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:193
msgid ""
"Such tools are essential if your package primarily focuses on providing "
"data access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:195
msgid "Some tools provide distributed access to larger data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:197
msgid ""
"**[DataLad](https://www.datalad.org/)** - Distributed data management for"
" scientific datasets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:199
msgid "Industry data engineering tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:200
msgid ""
"**[Git LFS](https://git-lfs.github.io/)** - Git extension for versioning "
"large files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:201
msgid ""
"**[DVC](https://dvc.org/)** - Data version control for machine learning "
"projects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:202
msgid ""
"**[Pachyderm](https://www.pachyderm.com/)** - Data pipeline platform with"
" version control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:205
msgid "Field specific standards + metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tests/package-data.md:208
msgid ""
"When creating data for your package, be aware of field-specific standards"
" and formats. For example, in neuroscience, DANDI and NWB are common file"
" formats used in the domain. So consider whether your package can / "
"should support those formats if you expect users in the neuroscience "
